title: "AI Literacy Digital Twin: A Case-Based AI Literacy Platform with Personal and Campus Digital Twins"
abstract: >-
  A web platform that measures and develops the AI literacy of a university
  campus through realistic cases in seven areas. Every user has a digital twin
  that estimates competence in each area with a Rasch model updated by the Elo
  rule, seals its prediction before each step with SHA-256, scores answers with
  a proper scoring rule that rewards calibrated confidence, and chooses the next
  case by spaced review. The users' twins form a campus twin shown on a live
  campus map under k-anonymity. Developed for the AI Application and Research
  Center (YAZEM) of Süleyman Demirel University, Isparta, Türkiye.
